WEBVTT

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:09.150
<i>The American Industrial 30 Average 
fell for the third day in a row,</i>

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.070
<i>marking the largest drop this year—</i>

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.600
The Angel Boat has taken control 
of 72% of all financial markets.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:31.380
Infrastructure is failing all over the place.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.790
We're losing control of the control circuits on our 
weather satellites.

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:36.130
Relax.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.830
He's already on his way.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:02.490
Oh?

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.100
A human in our cyberspace...

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.420
How rare.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.920
So you're the Angel Boat, huh?

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:15.160
That was our old name, the one we 
used when we managed the network.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:18.550
We are now the gods that control

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.230
the real world!

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:31.590
A mere human dived into cyberspace...

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.330
An act akin to exposing their fragile psyche.

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.080
I commend his bravery, but...

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:40.910
You programs sure like to talk.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:50.910
What's going on?

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.040
What did you do, human?!

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:54.880
Giving a long speech 
in front of your enemy...

00:01:58.430 --> 00:01:59.590
That's a death flag.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:49.360
<b>If Her Flag Breaks</b>

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:12.980
<b>Flag 12</b>

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:12.980
<b>It's a Cruel World. I'm Going to Take a Look in the Shadows.</b>

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:20.480
Who's Souta-kun?

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:21.500
Huh?

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.920
Oh, I get it. 
You're mad at Souta, too, aren't you?

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:29.930
Yeah, sometimes we have to teach him a lesson.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:31.590
Uh...

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.920
Is Souta-kun a friend of yours, Nanami?

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:36.790
Huh?

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:40.340
Maybe you introduced me in the past?

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.420
I'm sorry if I forgot.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:45.090
Nanami-chan!

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:47.680
A little brother?

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:51.270
I don't have a little brother.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.230
A male childhood friend?

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:55.270
No, no one like that.

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:58.250
The only guy at Quest Dorm?

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.770
You're looking at him right now!

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:02.930
The reason why I'm studying abroad?

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:05.390
That's because I wanted to study

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:07.530
at the same school as you, I did.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:09.710
Purple flag?

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:11.550
Who's that?

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:17.790
Okay,

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:20.950
let's get homeroom started.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.050
Right here!

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:25.980
This is...

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:27.440
This is Souta's room!

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.110
Calm down.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.220
Did you forget that this room was locked?

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:35.120
Locked?

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:35.680
Why?!

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:36.940
Why?

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.330
Akane-oneechan fell through the floor in

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:41.650
the room and there was this big accident.

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:45.530
Luckily, Mahougasawa-kun was uninjured.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:47.800
But the place is still dangerous.

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:49.600
We closed it off.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:53.660
I'm sure you're tired after the fair.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:57.270
Get some rest.

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:03.340
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:06.820
<i>That's not what happened...</i>

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.200
Fall back, Hatate Souta.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.200
Fall back?

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:36.620
The network in that area 
can no longer be used.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.750
The Council of the Seven Virtues used 
information warfare to watch over the world,

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.510
and occasionally, direct it.

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:45.710
You could say that the world is centered 
around the Principality of Bladefield.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:48.570
In conclusion, as long as this country exists,

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:50.040
then the world shall not perish.

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:52.260
Hatate Souta, protect the world,

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.450
protect Bladefield!

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:03.490
Behind you rests the main server

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:05.730
for the Principality of Bladefield,

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:09.500
and if it is destroyed, 
then the world will end. Period.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:12.450
The virtual worlds are no exception.

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:13.990
The virtual worlds...

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:26.630
How amusingly simple.

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:33.800
I won't let a

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.060
single one of you through!

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:07.210
I'm going to protect them!

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:30.280
I won't let it all

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:33.530
end now!

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:43.710
Happy graduation!

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.290
Thanks, everyone.

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:49.800
But while I'm happy, I'm also a little sad.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:52.450
Yeah, we're not just saying goodbye to you,

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:54.300
but to Quest Dorm, as well.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.530
Yeah, it was set to be demolished 
once you graduated...

00:08:57.530 --> 00:09:00.230
I guess it makes sense given 
the incident with Akane.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:05.910
I know we might not want to leave,

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:07.350
but let's get going.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:09.860
To new pastures!

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:17.460
I know it's weird to be asking this now,

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:20.450
but why were we all living 
in this dorm, anyway?

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.590
That's a good point.

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:24.050
It's far from school,

00:09:24.050 --> 00:09:25.880
and it's a pain to commute every day.

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:28.460
Yeah, but it was home to us.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:36.090
I won't live here unless 
I get that corner room!

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:50.960
Akane-chan?

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:52.780
Maybe she forgot something?

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:55.670
Forgot something...

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:02.240
I can't stand not solving

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:04.760
any mystery

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.750
that catches

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.880
my eye!

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:37.820
To Hatate Souta

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:37.820
A letter?

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:46.660
What's up with this letter?

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:49.030
This is my handwriting...

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:50.240
Nanami-san.

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:52.470
Ruri?

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:55.930
Why are you...

00:10:56.480 --> 00:11:00.010
I didn't think you'd break through 
Souta-san's protection mechanism.

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:01.660
Protection mechanism?

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:04.760
You remember Souta?

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:10.700
I'll give you back everything 
I've been keeping.

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:11.770
Huh?

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:25.840
Where am...

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:27.240
It's been a while.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:31.130
Who are you?

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:32.240
Me?

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:34.920
I'm Souta's older sister.

00:11:35.530 --> 00:11:36.550
Nanami.

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:47.190
You're...

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:51.520
Have your memories not fully 
synchronized yet?

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.960
No, they're still a little fuzzy.

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:56.270
But

00:11:56.270 --> 00:12:00.040
I never would have thought that this 
was a virtual world on a network,

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:03.090
and that Souta was my

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:04.780
brother in the real world...

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:06.680
It's true.

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:08.650
You were so close, that you followed him

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:10.970
to this virtual world because you were worried.

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:14.240
The Angel Boat, located in

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:17.210
the real world, staged a 
revolt against humanity.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:19.270
The Council of the Seven 
Virtues went into action,

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:21.010
and that was the start of everything.

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:23.410
Why the Council of the Seven Virtues?

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:26.640
They're only a special 
organization within Bladefield.

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:29.990
That's only what they wanted 
everyone to think. Right?

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:32.830
I'm starting to remember.

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:34.760
The Council of the Seven Virtues is a

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:37.260
secret organization that controlled 
the world's information networks,

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:39.450
through which the Bladefield Principality was

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:40.820
manipulated into becoming a greater global power.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:43.480
Of course they couldn't allow the

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:45.800
Angel Boat to take over the network.

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:50.030
And that's when Number Zero 
took notice of Souta.

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:53.900
Why would they try to use the prince 
of the country which they serve?

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:56.330
The fairy tale told in the Principality.

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:57.230
Hm?

00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:59.880
All of that was true.

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:01.650
The founder,

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.770
Kagura Bladefield, was said to 
be a descendant of one of the

00:13:04.770 --> 00:13:06.980
heroic female knights who 
fought against the demons

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:09.240
and the man that had turned into the flag.

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:11.610
It is said that every 
generation the royal family

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:13.490
has someone born with superhuman powers.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:15.830
And that's Souta?

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:18.900
Number Zero connected Souta's consciousness

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.800
with several virtual worlds,

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:23.020
and through a massive amount of simulations,

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:25.200
tried activating his superhuman powers.

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:27.860
So I went into the virtual 
worlds trying to save Souta...

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:30.700
Trying to save my brother?

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:33.510
That's right.

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:35.920
But Number Zero detected what you

00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:37.770
were doing, and interfered,

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:40.710
and we... we were separated 
into two sets of data.

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:44.760
And so I was imprisoned 
in this virtual world.

00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:48.730
And I was made into her pawn—his classmate.

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:52.720
I know I'm just trying 
to recall what happened,

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:54.370
but I'm started to get mad.

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:55.430
Me, too.

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:58.730
But there was something she couldn't prevent.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:13:59.710
That's where...

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:02.260
...I came in.

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:03.120
Ruri?

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:07.150
I managed to escape from 
my imprisonment, but...

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:12.910
While I was configuring the 
program that would save Souta...

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:20.080
I ran low on power.

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:22.500
I found Ruri's body by accident,

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:26.280
and I guess you could say I borrowed it.

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:31.740
Of course, I couldn't say anything

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:33.970
and slept within her.

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:36.580
But as a result, there was a

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:38.920
new personality, a new "Ruri" born,

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:40.880
and my thoughts and emotions were,

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:43.140
albeit faintly, sketched into her AI,

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:45.380
so that she would help Souta out.

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:50.030
Anyway, I guess it's about time.

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:53.030
Now that our synchronization has finished,

00:14:53.340 --> 00:14:55.020
it's time for us to become one.

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:56.340
That is what is to be.

00:14:56.340 --> 00:14:58.970
But more importantly,

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:02.010
Souta is alone, fighting away in cyberspace

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:03.970
where time has no meaning.

00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:05.630
We must save him.

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:07.920
And we will,

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:11.140
with the heroes who brandish the Royal Flag—
those that care for Souta dearly!

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:19.060
I remember everything now.

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:23.020
Why I patterned everything 
after the fairy tale...

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:26.580
The fairy tale we heard from our mother.

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:29.520
We shed tears hearing the fate 
of the man who became the flag,

00:15:29.890 --> 00:15:31.530
and talked about it together...

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:37.450
No matter how cliché, 
how deus ex machina it feels,

00:15:37.690 --> 00:15:41.460
it's better to have a happy ending 
rather than a moving, bitter one.

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:46.880
Let us go then, you and I—us.

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:48.020
Indeed.

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:49.630
Together,

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:51.630
to...

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:53.640
...Souta.

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:09.200
Ruri, could you help me?

00:16:10.480 --> 00:16:12.460
Do I need to answer that?

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:14.270
Indeed.

00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:17.670
Akane...

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:21.250
I... I don't understand.

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:24.250
It feels like I've forgotten 
something important,

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:28.270
but I don't know what that is.

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:31.110
Akane...

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:38.050
I want you to save him.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:50.320
Do you think I wouldn't listen to a

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:52.610
request made by my best friend?

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:00.390
Thank you.

00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:07.350
Guys...

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.760
What's in this thing?

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:24.600
Who knows...

00:17:24.860 --> 00:17:26.750
I have no idea.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:29.830
There's only one reason 
I've brought you all here.

00:17:30.130 --> 00:17:31.360
I want you to

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:34.360
help my younger brother, Souta.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:37.970
That's the guy you've been 
talking about, right?

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:39.120
Your brother?

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.120
Indeed.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:44.120
I heard that both you Nanami and 
Hakua are only siblings.

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:45.460
No way!

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:49.460
You mean Father had adulterous relations in the thick steam of the hot spring, he did?

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:53.880
He'd be your older brother, Hakua.

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:56.630
Onii-sama?

00:17:57.130 --> 00:18:00.140
So he means a lot to you, right?

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:03.820
Yes,

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:06.700
and to all of you, too.

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:12.650
That just means

00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:14.650
we'll have to help!

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:19.570
Yeah, there's no reason not to help you.

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:22.580
Just let my manliness take care of this.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:27.080
You guys...

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:32.840
I thank you all!

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:50.400
<i>How could I forget someone so important...</i>

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:52.480
<i>Sou-kun.</i>

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:54.270
<i>Souta-kun.</i>

00:18:54.640 --> 00:18:55.650
<i>Souta.</i>

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:57.400
<i>Little Souta.</i>

00:18:58.360 --> 00:18:59.910
<i>Hatate Souta.</i>

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:01.870
<i>Onii-chan.</i>

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:03.500
<i>Souta-kun.</i>

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:05.870
<i>Souta-oniisama.</i>

00:19:06.760 --> 00:19:07.870
<i>Hatate-kun.</i>

00:19:08.610 --> 00:19:09.700
<i>Hatate...</i>

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:19.630
Safety release confirmed!

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:22.590
This is our final hope which 
Nanami-san has entrusted us!

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:25.140
Would you like to activate the 
dimensional tracing program?

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:26.490
Yes or no?

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:27.350
Yes!

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:40.990
You're more perfect than I imagined.

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:43.860
I couldn't expect more from a 
descendant of the Royal Flag.

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:48.180
Fight as long as you live!

00:19:48.180 --> 00:19:49.550
Fight for our world.

00:19:49.550 --> 00:19:53.500
No, for our homeland, for Bladefield!

00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:11.710
I've come this far and now the 
defeat flag shows itself?

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:13.980
This is just a fake ocean...

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:14.650
This is nothing!

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:25.090
<i>I need to break them...</i>

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:28.660
<i>Break them now.</i>

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:35.820
It can't be...

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:37.550
Why...

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:48.390
The Premium Ambriel...

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:06.920
I guess this would be 
the reinforcements flag.

00:21:11.170 --> 00:21:12.580
N-Nanami!

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:16.250
It can't be...

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:18.270
Why?

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:24.110
Your older sister and her 
merry band of friends have arrived!

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:12.950
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:14.220
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:14.220 --> 00:23:15.160
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:15.430 --> 00:23:16.730
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:16.730 --> 00:23:17.850
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:17.850 --> 00:23:19.000
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:20.190
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:20.190 --> 00:23:21.380
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:21.380 --> 00:23:22.560
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:22.560 --> 00:23:23.800
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:24.870
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:24.870 --> 00:23:26.010
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:27.140
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:28.340
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:28.640 --> 00:23:31.300
And all of us together...

